From: MaSi <noreply@masi.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8550: add a PCIe suspend OPP

Armada 0520. 1000 kBps floor so AOP still has a PCIe memory-path sleep vote.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi	2026-09-29 15:43:48.683974720 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi	2026-09-29 15:43:48.684132062 +0200
@@ -2464,6 +2464,18 @@
 					opp-peak-kBps = <1969000 1>;
 					opp-level = <3>;
 				};
+
+				/*
+				 * Suspend-only DDR/LLCC floor for the RPMh sleep
+				 * set. opp-hz is synthetic and opp-level is
+				 * absent, so link-speed matching cannot select it.
+				 */
+				opp-suspend-1 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_min_svs>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <1000 1>;
+					opp-suspend;
+				};
 			};
 
 			pcieport0: pcie@0 {
